        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1f907eb3-6a85-3a8b-8683-f2d9ce789541",
                "word": "bigorexie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f086f120-ddc6-4e21-866e-1439f0bd03e1",
                        "entry_id": "1f907eb3-6a85-3a8b-8683-f2d9ce789541",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bigorexies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e288f051-9ded-31f6-87bc-d4ff562ef775",
                        "entry_id": "1f907eb3-6a85-3a8b-8683-f2d9ce789541",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dépendance excessive d’un être humain à l’activité sportive, notamment pour développer sa masse musculaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Nosologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff9bf0ce-915e-47e0-8c00-a8058cb0c3f0",
                                "sense_id": "e288f051-9ded-31f6-87bc-d4ff562ef775",
                                "text": "En septembre 2011, l'Organisation mondiale de la santé (OMS) reconnaît officiellement la bigorexie.\nLa bigorexie touche toute personne pratiquant une activité sportive à trop forte dose pour son corps."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae8b9f91-21b1-4de2-aae7-d5ac550d6557",
                                "sense_id": "e288f051-9ded-31f6-87bc-d4ff562ef775",
                                "text": "Au-delà de ces conclusions l’addiction au sport est récemment devenue une maladie : la bigorexie est officiellement reconnue par l’Organisation mondiale de la Santé (OMS) depuis septembre 2011."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a907659-9dd0-4ffd-a55f-c08e18bf28e4",
                                "sense_id": "e288f051-9ded-31f6-87bc-d4ff562ef775",
                                "text": "On parle de bigorexie, explique Yves St-Louis, \"quand le sport devient une drogue\"."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3f931d5b-29f1-42dc-97b1-a60e3851b2c1",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f907eb3-6a85-3a8b-8683-f2d9ce789541",
                        "source_sense_id": "e288f051-9ded-31f6-87bc-d4ff562ef775",
                        "source_sense_description": "Dépendance excessive à l’activité sportive",
                        "target_lang_word": "bigorexia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bigorexia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4f9a0e7-c5af-36da-b052-0dc7148f17eb",
                                        "entry_id": "e4733f54-daf8-3d46-9dda-986fdaac63c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mental disorder in which the sufferer perceives himself to have inadequate musculature; most common among bodybuilders"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7e5c7d1-f2e0-4076-8937-977187e1cd8e",
                                                "sense_id": "d4f9a0e7-c5af-36da-b052-0dc7148f17eb",
                                                "text": "The quest for perfect pecs is so strong that psychiatrists now sometimes refer to it as “bigorexia,” a form of muscle dysmorphia exhibited mostly by men and characterized by excessive weight lifting, a preoccupation with not feeling muscular enough and a strict adherence to eating foods that lower weight and build muscle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "694661e3-0307-4751-8f98-f3e799683edd",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f907eb3-6a85-3a8b-8683-f2d9ce789541",
                        "source_sense_id": "e288f051-9ded-31f6-87bc-d4ff562ef775",
                        "source_sense_description": "Dépendance excessive à l’activité sportive",
                        "target_lang_word": "vigorexia",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vigorexia",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b4fe3c4-2f17-32f2-8427-95e86e00e2f1",
                                        "entry_id": "b0090615-7664-3b11-8dad-073d88ac7a0d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Trastorno caracterizado por la presencia de una preocupación obsesiva por el físico y una distorsión del esquema corporal (dismorfofobia). Implica una adicción a la actividad física (especialmente a la musculación)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Enfermedades"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22eaf141-4f37-472c-a69b-e294bb096095",
                                                "sense_id": "3b4fe3c4-2f17-32f2-8427-95e86e00e2f1",
                                                "text": "Y creemos habría que prestar mayor atención no sólo desde la óptica de los trastornos asociados (vigorexia, anorexia, abuso de esteroides-anabolizantes, etc…) sino desde la vertiente de la psicología de la normalidad y de los procesos básicos, como forma de mejorar el rendimiento de estos atletas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75bec8c7-7013-4876-a6ab-19302313fe69",
                                                "sense_id": "3b4fe3c4-2f17-32f2-8427-95e86e00e2f1",
                                                "text": "nuevos contenidos asociados a lo viril han generado —entre otras cosas— un mercado creciente de cosmética para hombres y desórdenes paralelos a la anorexia (mayoritaria pero no exclusivamente femenina) como la musculación compulsiva o vigorexia."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
